# Shot-by-shot design references, v2

**Current IDs: 127 total.** This reference package is keyed to `direction/shotlist.csv` at director commit `b64694758829`: picture S001–S126 and editorial credits S127. The prior director 131-shot numbering (`69379be`, release `direction-v2`) and our corresponding `design-shot-reference-v1` release are **superseded**. All picture deliverables should use these 127 shot IDs, which align with editor v0 and DP’s `picture/shot-log.json`; the director's `obs` column records earlier observation IDs. Full source time 00:00.00–10:58.32.

`design/shot-reference-index.csv` gives each shot's scene, source in/out/midpoint, reference still name, scene design family, design-file pointer and director framing/camera/content. Release `design-shot-reference-v2` carries six indexed contact sheets and 127 full-resolution midpoint studies in one ZIP. Each picture ID S001–S126 has its own frame. S127 is credits owned by editor; its still is for design continuity, not a picture deliverable. Source: Orange Open Movie Project / Blender Foundation, *Elephants Dream* (2006), CC BY 2.5.

**Source images are reference ONLY:** never splice, trace, filter, upscale or composite these pixels into finished picture. A still does not depict an entire moving shot: very short shots or dissolves may show blur, fades or intermediate phases. Study the full frozen film between the given in/out times and director's `direction/shotlist.csv` (some shots combine several observation beats) before constructing a wholly new drawing or render. Scene design families follow `direction/direction-notes.md` at `b646947`, not an image classifier. `design/bible.md` locks repeatable character/place details and `design/opening-wall.md` locks S001.

The reference extractor is `tools/build_shot_reference_index.py` (imageio-ffmpeg with FFmpeg 7.0.2-static; Pillow 13.0.0). Sampled input is the frozen 326,632,467-byte film in `production-designer`#1, SHA-256 `a462c56d921fb24bbdde02470b34ee4ca8e866bde938090791e13207db39136c`.
